experts in Italy have authenticated a  painting that vanished more than two  decades ago Gustav Klimt portrait of a  lady was discovered in December and  Friday evening authorities announced the  results of their investigation Seth  Doane reports from Rome it was a missing  masterpiece a decades-old mystery in the  art world and while many questions still  remain a big one was it real has now  been answered there she was against her  green background looking as if nothing  had happened yet I'd like to say with no  lack of emotion that I can announce the  painting is authentic prosecutor or  nella chica told press Friday this  priceless piece portrait of a lady  painted around 1916 by the Austrian  master Gustav Klimt had gone missing  from a gallery in the Italian city of  Piacenza nearly 23 years ago  then in December Italian police were  called to the scene after a gardener at  the same gallery had get this cleared  away ivy revealing a small door and a  hole in a wall inside was a plastic bag  with the masterpiece Klimt best-known  work may be the kiss but his love and  appreciation for women and their beauty  is seen throughout his art where he  often painted socialites in Vienna with  a seductive tenderness something rather  romantic about an art theft even though  in a very practical sense it's probably  the most foolish kind of robbery to have  colors vary Robert Simon is in New York  art historian and dealer who suggests  one problem for thieves may have been  how easily identifiable this was this is  a there's a famous painting well  documented so to sell it it's kind of an  impractical idea adding to the value of  this work and helping to authenticate it  is that Klimt painted this lady on top  of another one there is a second  portrait underneath our investigators  will hold on to that portrait for a  while longer to carry out additional  tests to see if it holds more clues  including who might have stolen it  for CBS this morning Saturday Seth Doane  row